{"id": 92, "ts": 1783828254.9064214, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1 that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest overall fit. While Candidate\u202fC shows impressive situational awareness\u2014anticipating danger, seeing complex connections, and strong leadership\u2014my request to Markus for any evidence of stress\u2011resilience came back empty. Without proof that C can stay calm and effective under high\u2011pressure events, we cannot rely on his leadership alone for long\u2011distance flights. Candidate\u202fA\u2019s flawless reliability and quick decision\u2011making are offset by his poor communication, egocentric attitude, and low willingness to continue learning, which jeopardise crew cooperation and adaptability. Candidate\u202fD demonstrates solid technical problem\u2011solving and responsibility, yet we still lack evidence of his operational reliability and his moody, loner demeanor raises red flags for crew interaction. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB is documented to handle stress very well, is very conscientious, assesses weather accurately, and possesses excellent computer skills\u2014key for the technical and decision\u2011quality demands of international routes. Although B can be pretentious and occasionally uses the wrong tone, these communication issues appear less critical than the missing stress\u2011resilience evidence for C and the broader concerns for A and D. Therefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
