{"id": 99, "ts": 1783828309.9268878, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the thorough recap, especially the emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress handling and technical skills. However, the lack of any concrete example of B\u2019s decision\u2011quality under pressure remains a critical gap. In a long\u2011distance role, the ability to make accurate, timely safety\u2011critical decisions is non\u2011negotiable, and we have no evidence that B has demonstrated this.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC brings strong situational awareness\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, and possessing excellent spatial vision\u2014combined with very good leadership qualities. While C is seen as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas, these concerns affect crew cooperation but do not directly undermine the core safety competencies we need. Moreover, the absence of stress\u2011resilience data for C is noted, yet the same level of missing evidence exists for B\u2019s decision quality, which is arguably more decisive for flight safety.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC offers the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot position, provided we address the minor concerns about openness and attitude through targeted onboarding."}
